40:  * To create a promise, use the {@link Promise#async(Upstream)} method (or one of the variants such as {@link Promise#sync(Factory)}.
41:  * To test code that uses promises, use the {@link ratpack.test.exec.ExecHarness}.
42:  * <p>
43:  * The promise is not “activated” until the {@link #then(Action)} method is called.
44:  * This method terminates the pipeline, and receives the final value.
45:  * <p>
46:  * Promise objects are multi use.
47:  * Every promise pipeline has a value producing function at its start.
48:  * Activating a promise (i.e. calling {@link #then(Action)}) invokes the function.
